target
# Crash/timeout/OOM reproducers cargo-fuzz writes here on a failure.
# Deliberately ignored: per the P1.9.3 acceptance criterion "every crash
# becomes a permanent regression test", a real find belongs in
# corpus/<target>/ (copy it there and commit it) rather than living only
# in this ephemeral, unreviewed directory.
artifacts
coverage
# The 24 h campaign's own scratch corpus and logs (see README.md's
# "24-hour pre-M1.5 campaign" section) -- large, one-machine-specific, and
# never meant to be committed wholesale. A real find is promoted by hand:
# copy the one artifact (or corpus entry) that matters into corpus/<target>/
# below and commit *that*.
campaign-logs
campaign-corpus
# fuzz/corpus/<target>/ is INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored: it holds the
# checked-in seed corpus (see seed_corpus.py) plus any crash-derived
# regression a developer has promoted into it. Every command in README.md
# passes an explicit scratch corpus directory when actually fuzzing (as
# opposed to replaying), so this directory should stay exactly the curated
# set checked in here -- if `git status` ever shows unexpected new files
# under it, a command was run without its scratch-dir argument.
